{"authoredAt":"2026-08-24T10:08:18.735Z","conclusion":"findings","findings":[{"category":"missing","desc":"doc-code-drift: docs/host-run-usage.md:64-65 says the canonical Story worktree is the durable root for the sealed run, output journal, and terminal receipt, but packages/main/src/core/runtime-artifact-registry.ts:23-26 resolves shared runtime ownership to the primary worktree and packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts:640-645 stores runs and receipt archives there. This directs operators to a linked Story worktree that may be removed at DONE instead of the actual durable runtime location. [severity=medium]","evidenceState":"verified","files":["docs/host-run-usage.md","packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts","packages/main/src/core/runtime-artifact-registry.ts"],"severity":"medium"},{"category":"missing","desc":"doc-code-drift: docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md:85 names the durable capability artifact as `input.capability`, while packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts:890 persists it as `input.cap` and runtime diagnostics also inspect `input.cap`. The backticked exact artifact name is incorrect. [severity=medium]","evidenceState":"verified","files":["docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md","packages/main/src/core/managed-host-run.ts"],"severity":"medium"},{"category":"missing","desc":"doc-code-drift: docs/host-run-usage.md:395 and docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md:121,136 define `adapter_only` as a low-level adapter whose caller owns admission, but packages/main/src/core/provider-process-registry.ts:543 classifies core/host-run.ts as `adapter_only` while packages/main/src/core/host-run.ts:2073 and 2215 acquire provider admission inside runHostRun itself. The documented status meaning is not true for every registry member. [severity=medium]","evidenceState":"verified","files":["docs/host-run-usage.md","docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md","packages/main/src/core/host-run.ts","packages/main/src/core/provider-process-registry.ts"],"severity":"medium"},{"category":"missing","desc":"doc-code-drift: docs/host-run-usage.md:396 and docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md:137 define `readiness_probe` as version/readiness probing only, but packages/main/src/core/provider-process-registry.ts:548-568 assigns that status to Git/process verification, finding reproduction, process ancestry, evidence checks, and configured lint execution. The documented category is substantially narrower than its implemented inventory semantics. [severity=medium]","evidenceState":"verified","files":["docs/host-run-usage.md","docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md","packages/main/src/core/provider-process-registry.ts"],"severity":"medium"}],"lane":"lattice-review-docs","providerAgent":"lattice-review-docs","readLog":{"digest":"975fd5762f3633e87ae36e844b62a96722c750afe28701cd0c3849eb10ccdd2c","filesReadFully":["docs/requirements/decisions/managed-cross-provider-cli-execution.md","docs/requirements/decisions/review-assurance-floor-execution-plan.md","docs/requirements/decisions/review-run-binding-race.md"],"filesTriagedByName":["docs/requirements/decisions/cli-engine-english-open-source-execution-plan.md","docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-authority-live-integration.md","docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-codex-command-boundary-execution-plan.md","docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-llm-usage-ledger-execution-plan.md","docs/requirements/decisions/lattice-midflight-story-repair-and-gitroot-worktree-plan.md","docs/requirements/decisions/multi-host-keyword-candidate-spec-routing-execution-plan.md","docs/requirements/decisions/proof-admissibility-hardening-execution-plan.md","docs/requirements/decisions/proof-or-stop-agent-prompt-consolidation-execution-plan.md","docs/requirements/decisions/proof-or-stop-thin-entrypoint-contract-migration-execution-plan.md","docs/r